          "grounding_supports": [
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 158,
                "end_index": 260,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Historically, the NFL had very rigid numbering rules to help referees easily identify player positions"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 262,
                "end_index": 325,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "However, in recent years, those rules have been heavily relaxed"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 340,
                "end_index": 461,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Modern NFL Rules (Current)\nUnder the current NFL rulebook, linebackers have immense flexibility with their jersey choices"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 340,
                "end_index": 514,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Modern NFL Rules (Current)\nUnder the current NFL rulebook, linebackers have immense flexibility with their jersey choices:\n* **Allowed Numbers:** **0 to 59** and **90 to 99**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                4,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 516,
                "end_index": 744,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **The Rule Changes:** \n  * In **2021**, the NFL relaxed its rules, allowing linebackers to wear single digits, teens, 20s, 30s, and 40s (which were previously reserved for quarterbacks, specialists, and skill position players)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 748,
                "end_index": 908,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* In **2023**, the league approved the use of the number **0**, which several prominent linebackers immediately adopted (such as Roquan Smith and Ivan Pace Jr.)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 918,
                "end_index": 1066,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Historical/Classic NFL Ranges\nIf you are looking for the \"classic\" aesthetic of a linebacker, they traditionally wore numbers in two distinct ranges"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 918,
                "end_index": 1188,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Historical/Classic NFL Ranges\nIf you are looking for the \"classic\" aesthetic of a linebacker, they traditionally wore numbers in two distinct ranges:\n* **50\u201359 (The Original Standard):** Standardized in 1973, this is the classic range for middle and inside linebackers"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1190,
                "end_index": 1378,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **90\u201399 (Added in 1984):** When the 3-4 defense (utilizing four linebackers, including two outside pass-rushers) became highly popular in the 1980s, teams ran out of numbers in the 50s"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1380,
                "end_index": 1434,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The NFL opened up the 90s to linebackers to solve this"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1444,
                "end_index": 1714,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Iconic Linebacker Numbers (Classic Era)\nSome of the greatest defensive players in NFL history have made certain numbers deeply synonymous with the linebacker position:\n* **#51:** **Dick Butkus** (Chicago Bears) \u2014 The ultimate old-school, hard-hitting middle linebacker"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1716,
                "end_index": 1855,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **#52:** **Ray Lewis** (Baltimore Ravens) & **Patrick Willis** (San Francisco 49ers) \u2014 The modern gold standards for inside linebackers"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1857,
                "end_index": 1994,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **#54:** **Brian Urlacher** (Chicago Bears) & **Bobby Wagner** (Seattle Seahawks) \u2014 Known for speed and sideline-to-sideline tackling"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10,
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1996,
                "end_index": 2141,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **#55:** **Junior Seau** (San Diego Chargers) & **Derrick Brooks** (Tampa Bay Buccaneers) \u2014 Hall of Fame leaders of their respective defenses"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2143,
                "end_index": 2277,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **#56:** **Lawrence Taylor** (New York Giants) \u2014 Arguably the most feared defensive player and iconic jersey number in NFL history"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                9,
                11
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2279,
                "end_index": 2470,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **#58:** **Jack Lambert** (Pittsburgh Steelers), **Derrick Thomas** (Kansas City Chiefs), & **Von Miller** (Denver Broncos) \u2014 The premier number for elite pass-rushing outside linebackers"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2472,
                "end_index": 2556,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **#59:** **Luke Kuechly** (Carolina Panthers) & **Jack Ham** (Pittsburgh Steelers)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                12
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2571,
                "end_index": 2772,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "College Football (NCAA) Traditions\nUnlike the NFL, college football does not have strict positional rules for numbers (any player who isn't an offensive lineman can wear almost any number from 0 to 99)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                13,
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2774,
                "end_index": 3026,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "However, two famous college programs have highly respected linebacker number traditions:\n* **Penn State's \"St1x C1ty\" (#11):** At Penn State (often called \"Linebacker U\"), the number 11 is reserved for the team's most elite, culture-defining linebacker"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                15,
                13
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3028,
                "end_index": 3170,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This tradition was popularized by LaVar Arrington and has since been passed down to stars like NaVorro Bowman, Micah Parsons, and Abdul Carter"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                16,
                17
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3172,
                "end_index": 3259,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **USC's \"55 Club\" (#55):** The Trojan defense does not hand out the number 55 lightly"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                18,
                16,
                17
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3261,
                "end_index": 3432,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "It is only awarded to game-changing, highly touted linebackers, a tradition established by Junior Seau and carried on by Willie McGinest, Chris Claiborne, and Keith Rivers"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
          ],
